ce_calibration\\\\n  text: NER reasonably well-calibrated (calibration ECE 0.069-0.096), RE shows greater\\\\n    miscalibration (ECE 0.109-0.339)\\\\n  sections:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  tier: 1\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap\\\\n    metric: calibration_ece\\\\n    value:\\\\n      ner_range: 0.069-0.096\\\\n      re_range: 0.109-0.339\\\\n  note: Previous c016 used binary ECE (0.27-0.77) which was incorrect metric. Calibration\\\\n    ECE (signal confidence → mean F1 deviation) shows NER is well-calibrated, RE has\\\\n    moderate miscalibration. Consistent with fig_reliability_1024.\\\\n- id: c017_fisher_z_ner_vs_re\\\\n  text: 'Fisher''s z-test ρ_SJ NER vs RE: z=2.31, p=0.021'\\\\n  sections:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  tier: 1\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_004_re_diagnostic\\\\n    metric: fisher_z_ner_vs_re.sj_z\\\\n    value: 2.31\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_004_re_diagnostic\\\\n    metric: fisher_z_ner_vs_re.sj_p\\\\n    value: 0.0209\\\\n- id: c018_per_relation_diagnostic\\\\n  text: Feature-Of ρ≈0.004, Hyponym-Of ρ=0.646\\\\n  sections:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  tier: 1\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_004_re_diagnostic\\\\n    metric: per_relation_type.FEATURE-OF.rho_sj\\\\n    value: 0.004\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_004_re_diagnostic\\\\n    metric: per_relation_type.HYPONYM-OF.rho_fk\\\\n    value: 0.646\\\\n- id: c019_entity_span_errors\\\\n  text: Entity span errors account for 55.5% of RE false negatives\\\\n  sections:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  tier: 1\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp_004_re_diagnostic\\\\n    metric: error_propagation\\\\n    value: head_error 17.7% + tail_error (derived) + head_tail_error 15.9% + full_error\\\\n      21.7% → entity span errors ~55.5%\\\\n  note: Computed from error_propagation breakdown in exp_004\\\\n- id: c020_capability_stratification_ner\\\\n  text: SJ ρ=0.547 on SciERC instances with 6+ entities, vs 0.415 for 1-2 entities\\\\n  sections:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  tier: 1\\\\n  evide