{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015X2NYdnRJ6effKNw6xHSY4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n2\t\n3\t\\usepackage[review]{acl}\n4\t\n5\t\\usepackage{times}\n6\t\\usepackage{latexsym}\n7\t\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n8\t\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n9\t\\usepackage{microtype}\n10\t\\usepackage{inconsolata}\n11\t\\usepackage{graphicx}\n12\t\\usepackage{booktabs}\n13\t\\usepackage{amsmath}\n14\t\\usepackage{amssymb}\n15\t\\usepackage{multirow}\n16\t\\usepackage{xcolor}\n17\t\\usepackage{subcaption}\n18\t\n19\t\\graphicspath{{figures/}}\n20\t\n21\t\\title{Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors:\\\\ The Correlation-Selection Gap in LLM-Based Named Entity Recognition}\n22\t\n23\t\\author{Anonymous}\n24\t\n25\t\\begin{document}\n26\t\\maketitle\n27\t\n28\t\\input{sections/abstract}\n29\t\\input{sections/introduction}\n30\t\\input{sections/related_work}\n31\t\\input{sections/method}\n32\t\\input{sections/experiments}\n33\t\\input{sections/discussion}\n34\t\\input{sections/conclusion}\n35\t\n36\t\\section*{Limitations}\n37\t\\input{sections/limitations}\n38\t\n39\t\\section*{Ethics Statement}\n40\tAll experiments use publicly available benchmarks (SciERC, CoNLL-2003, WNUT-17) and open-weight models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-4B, LLaMA-3.1-8B).\n41\tCoNLL-2003 is derived from the Reuters RCV1 corpus, which is available for research purposes under a NIST agreement; we use the standard research distribution.\n42\tNo new human data was collected or annotated for this study.\n43\tOur findings on signal limitations could inform more reliable deployment of IE systems by guiding practitioners toward appropriate confidence signals for their use case.\n44\tCode and data will be released upon acceptance at [anonymized URL].\n45\t\n46\t\\bibliography{references}\n47\t\n48\t\\appendix\n49\t\\input{sections/appendix}\n50\t\n51\t\\end{document}\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017PRpM9onjmwRJfggHKtQBz","session_id":"b72398d7-e431