: manakul2023selfcheckgpt\\\\n    category: self_consistency_reasoning\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: Uses cross-sample consistency for hallucination detection — if LLM knows a fact, samples are consistent; hallucinations\\\\n      diverge. Motivates our consistency-based quality signal for IE.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:cluster1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T15:47:22.188Z'\\\\n  wan2025rasc:\\\\n    title: 'Reasoning Aware Self-Consistency: Leveraging Reasoning Paths for Efficient LLM Sampling'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Guangya Wan\\\\n    - Yuqi Wu\\\\n    - Jie Chen\\\\n    - Sheng Li\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: NAACL 2025\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2025.naacl-long.184/\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2025.naacl-long.184\\\\n    bibtex_key: wan2025rasc\\\\n    category: self_consistency_reasoning\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: 'RASC: quality-aware selection using reasoning path assessment + consistency-driven stopping. Reduces samples\\\\n      by ~70%. Complements our approach of structured quality-aware aggregation.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:cluster1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T15:47:22.188Z'\\\\n  nedellec2026consistency:\\\\n    title: 'Consistency-accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction: empirical findings\\\\n      from plant-health data'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Claire Nédellec\\\\n    - Jingbo Xia\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: Genomics & Informatics\\\\n    url: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12888769/\\\\n    doi: 10.1186/s44342-025-00063-2\\\\n    bibtex_key: nedellec2026consistency\\\\n    category: consistency_structured_ie\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: 'Most direct competitor: systematically measures consistency-accuracy correlation for LLM-based entity and\\\\n      relation extraction on plant-health data, validating consistency as a reliability signal for structured IE.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  vashurin2025cocoa:\\\\n    title: 'Uncertainty Quantification for LLMs through Minimum Bayes Risk: Bridging Confidence and Consistency'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Roman Vashurin\\\\n    - Maiya Goloburda\\\\n    - Albina Ilina\\\\n    - Aleksandr Rubashevskii\\\\n    - Preslav Nakov\\\\n    - Artem Shelmanov\\\\n    - Maxim Panov\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: NeurIPS 2025\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.04964\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: vashurin2025cocoa\\\\n    category: consistency_structured_ie\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: CoCoA framework unifies token-level confidence and sample-level consistency via MBR for uncertainty quantification.\\\\n      Provides theoretical grounding for our dual-signal approach in structured IE.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  hobelsberger2025systematic:\\\\n    title: Systematic Evaluation of Uncertainty Estimation Methods in Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Christian Hobelsberger\\\\n    - Theresa Winner\\\\n    - Andreas Nawroth\\\\n    - Oliver Mitevski\\\\n    - Anna-Carolina Haensch\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv preprint\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.20460\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: hobelsberger2025systematic\\\\n    category: consistency_structured_ie\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: Systematic comparison of VCE, MSP, self-consistency, and CoCoA for LLM uncertainty estimation. Shows hybrid\\\\n      CoCoA yields best calibration, supporting our multi-signal aggregation design.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  geng2024confidence:\\\\n    title: A Survey of Confidence Estimation and Calibration in Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Jiahui Geng\\\\n    - Fengyu Cai\\\\n    - Yuxia Wang\\\\n    - Heinz Koeppl\\\\n    - Preslav Nakov\\\\n    - Iryna Gurevych\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: NAACL 2024\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.08298\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2024.naacl-long.366\\\\n    bibtex_key: geng2024confidence\\\\n    category: confidence_surveys\\\\n    role: survey\\\\n    relevance: Comprehensive survey of LLM confidence estimation and calibration techniques. Provides taxonomic context for\\\\n      positioning our consistency-based confidence approach within the broader landscape.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  wen2025know:\\\\n    title: 'Know Your Limits: A Survey of Abstention in Large Language Models'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Bingbing Wen\\\\n    - Jihan Yao\\\\n    - Shangbin Feng\\\\n    - Chenjun Xu\\\\n    - Yulia Tsvetkov\\\\n    - Bill Howe\\\\n    - Lucy Lu Wang\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: TACL 2025\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.18418\\\\n    doi: 10.1162/tacl_a_00754\\\\n    bibtex_key: wen2025know\\\\n    category: confidence_surveys\\\\n    role: supplementary\\\\n    relevance: 'Survey on LLM abstention from query, model, and human-values perspectives. Our consistency-based filtering\\\\n      can be viewed as a structured-IE-specific abstention mechanism. [SUPPLEMENTARY: overlaps with geng2024 main survey]'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  xia2025survey:\\\\n    title: A Survey of Uncertainty Estimation Methods on Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Zhiqiu Xia\\\\n    - Jinxuan Xu\\\\n    - Yuqian Zhang\\\\n    - Hang Liu\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: ACL Findings 2025\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2025.findings-acl.1101/\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: xia2025survey\\\\n    category: confidence_surveys\\\\n    role: supplementary\\\\n    relevance: 'Most comprehensive LLM uncertainty estimation survey with novel taxonomy (verbalizing, latent, consistency-based,\\\\n      semantic clustering). Directly contextualizes our method within the consistency-based branch. [SUPPLEMENTARY: overlaps\\\\n      with geng2024 main survey]'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  liu2025uqcalibration:\\\\n    title: 'Uncertainty Quantification and Confidence Calibration in Large Language Models: A Survey'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Xiaoou Liu\\\\n    - Tiejin Chen\\\\n    - Longchao Da\\\\n    - Chacha Chen\\\\n    - Zhen Lin\\\\n    - Hua Wei\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: KDD 2025\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.15850\\\\n    doi: 10.1145/3711896.3736569\\\\n    bibtex_key: liu2025uqcalibration\\\\n    category: confidence_surveys\\\\n    role: supplementary\\\\n    relevance: 'Survey analyzing UQ through input, reasoning, parameter, and prediction uncertainty dimensions. Complements\\\\n      other surveys with focus on calibration techniques applicable to our structured IE setting. [SUPPLEMENTARY: overlaps\\\\n      with geng2024 main survey]'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  kuhn2023semantic:\\\\n    title: 'Semantic Uncertainty: Linguistic Invariances for Uncertainty Estimation in Natural Language Generation'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Lorenz Kuhn\\\\n    - Yarin Gal\\\\n    - Sebastian Far