stimation.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  guo2017calibration:\\\\n    title: On Calibration of Modern Neural Networks\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Chuan Guo\\\\n    - Geoff Pleiss\\\\n    - Yu Sun\\\\n    - Kilian Q. Weinberger\\\\n    year: 2017\\\\n    venue: ICML 2017\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.04599\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: guo2017calibration\\\\n    category: uncertainty_calibration\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Seminal work showing modern neural networks are miscalibrated and proposing temperature scaling. Foundational\\\\n      reference for all calibration work including our LLM confidence calibration for IE.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  desai2020calibration:\\\\n    title: Calibration of Pre-trained Transformers\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Shrey Desai\\\\n    - Greg Durrett\\\\n    year: 2020\\\\n    venue: EMNLP 2020\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.07892\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.21\\\\n    bibtex_key: desai2020calibration\\\\n    category: uncertainty_calibration\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Shows pre-trained transformers (BERT, RoBERTa) are well-calibrated in-domain but degrade OOD. Bridges classical\\\\n      calibration to the transformer era, motivating our LLM-specific calibration analysis.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  kossen2024semantic:\\\\n    title: 'Semantic Entropy Probes: Robust and Cheap Hallucination Detection in LLMs'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Jannik Kossen\\\\n    - Jiatong Han\\\\n    - Muhammed Razzak\\\\n    - Lisa Schut\\\\n    - Shreshth Malik\\\\n    - Yarin Gal\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: arXiv preprint\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.15927\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: kossen2024semantic\\\\n    category: uncertainty_calibration\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: Proposes lightweight probes to approximate semantic entropy from hidden states of a single generation, reducing\\\\n      cost to near-zero. Relevant to our goal of efficient uncertainty estimation for structured IE.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  xiong2024verbalized:\\\\n    title: Can LLMs Express Their Uncertainty? An Empirical Evaluation of Confidence Elicitation in LLMs\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Miao Xiong\\\\n    - Zhiyuan Hu\\\\n    - Xinyang Lu\\\\n    - Yifei Li\\\\n    - Jie Fu\\\\n    - Junxian He\\\\n    - Bryan Hooi\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2024\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13063\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: xiong2024verbalized\\\\n    category: uncertainty_calibration\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: Systematic evaluation of verbalized confidence elicitation via prompting, sampling, and aggregation. Directly\\\\n      relevant to our use of LLM-expressed confidence as a signal for structured IE quality.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch1\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T17:52:10.000Z'\\\\n  fisch2021conformal:\\\\n    title: Few-Shot Conformal Prediction with Auxiliary Tasks\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Adam Fisch\\\\n    - Tal Schuster\\\\n    - Tommi Jaakkola\\\\n    - Regina Barzilay\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: ICML 2021\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.08898\\\\n    doi: 10.5555/3524938.3525234\\\\n    bibtex_key: fisch2021conformal\\\\n    category: conformal_prediction\\\\n    role: supplementary\\\\n    relevance: 'Adapts conformal prediction to few-shot settings via meta-learning over auxiliary tasks, producing tighter\\\\n      prediction sets with formal coverage guarantees. SUPPLEMENTARY - CP not a method component, angelopoulos2021 retained as main CP reference.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  angelopoulos2021conformal:\\\\n    title: Uncertainty Sets for Image Classifiers using Conformal Prediction\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Anastasios N. Angelopoulos\\\\n    - Stephen Bates\\\\n    - Jitendra Malik\\\\n    - Michael I. Jordan\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2021\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.14193\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: angelopoulos2021conformal\\\\n    category: conformal_prediction\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Introduces RAPS (Regularized Adaptive Prediction Sets) with finite-sample coverage guarantees. Foundation for\\\\n      conformal prediction methodology we adapt to structured IE output sets.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  bates2021rcps:\\\\n    title: Distribution-Free, Risk-Controlling Prediction Sets\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Stephen Bates\\\\n    - Anastasios Angelopoulos\\\\n    - Lihua Lei\\\\n    - Jitendra Malik\\\\n    - Michael I. Jordan\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: Journal of the ACM 2021\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02703\\\\n    doi: 10.1145/3478535\\\\n    bibtex_key: bates2021rcps\\\\n    category: conformal_prediction\\\\n    role: supplementary\\\\n    relevance: 'Generalizes conformal prediction to control arbitrary monotone losses for set-valued predictors with finite-sample\\\\n      guarantees. SUPPLEMENTARY - CP not a method component, angelopoulos2021 retained as main CP reference.'\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  xiao2019uncertainty:\\\\n    title: Quantifying Uncertainties in Natural Language Processing Tasks\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Yijun Xiao\\\\n    - William Yang Wang\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    venue: AAAI 2019\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.07253\\\\n    doi: 10.1609/aaai.v33i01.33017322\\\\n    bibtex_key: xiao2019uncertainty\\\\n    category: token_span_uncertainty_ner\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Pioneers Bayesian uncertainty quantification for NLP tasks including NER, showing that \\\\n\\\\n... [截断: 省略 23664 字符，传 max_chars=0 获取完整内容]\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 43664, \\\"truncated\\\": true}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017PRpM9onjmwRJfggHKtQBz","session_id":"b72398d7-e431-4137-b17e-51fc8746e976","uuid":"2402d1f3-7f2a-4949-b644-f93a4c3c7423","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:14:07.526Z"}
